course: dictionary
lesson: 7173
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Permit can be an action word (a verb) or a naming word (a noun). Ask yourself: is the word doing something, or is it a thing?
explain: In «many cities have rules or permits for it», permits are things you can hold, like an official paper that says you are allowed to do something. That is the noun. In «feathers of some protected birds may not be kept without a permit», permit is also a noun.
explain: As a verb, permit means to allow someone to do something. Test it by swapping in allow and checking that the sentence still makes sense. You will also see permit in the phrase weather permitting, which means if the weather allows it.
fact: Permit can be a verb: to allow someone to do something, or to make something possible.
fact: Permit can be a noun: an official paper that gives you permission to do something.
fact: The forms of the verb are permit, permits, permitted and permitting.
fact: «Busking» means performing in public places for tips.
fact: Weather permitting means if the weather allows it.
exercise: In «many cities have rules or permits for it», what is a permit? | *An official paper that gives you permission | To allow someone to do something | A type of weather | A kind of musical instrument
exercise: In «feathers of some protected birds may not be kept without a permit», is permit a noun or a verb? | *A noun, an official paper giving permission | A verb, meaning to pick up | A verb, meaning to keep safe | A noun, meaning a feather
exercise: Complete the phrase: We will go to the beach, weather ____. | permit | permitted | *permitting | permits
test: What does permit mean in «the rules permit us to sing»? | A loud noise | A feather | *To allow | A paper you must hold
test: What does «swimming is not permitted» mean? | Swimming is free | Swimming is very fast | Swimming is very loud | *Swimming is not allowed
exam: In «Busking means performing in public places for tips; many cities have rules or permits for it», which meaning of permit is used, and how do you know? | A verb, to make something possible | *A noun, an official paper, because cities have permits as things they give out | A noun, meaning a tip | A verb, to allow, because cities allow busking
